description.narrative:
The Government of Germany, in a joint initiative by the Federal Ministry of Interior, Building, and Community and the Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development, has committed to support UN-Habitat over a four-year cycle in promoting the principle of integrated sustainable urban development based on the New Urban Agenda as outlined in the UN-Habitat Strategic Plan 2020 – 2023, indicating the following broad areas of cooperation, which have subsequently been confirmed through an exchange of letters with the Executive Director: 
a) Support to the work on the implementation of the UN-Habitat Strategic Plan 2020 - 2023;
b) Dissemination of the objectives of the New Leipzig Charter and the New Urban Agenda as a basis for sustainable urban development;
c) Strengthening of the multilateral dialogue on the objectives and forms of implementation of national urban development policies.
In these three areas of support, the funding will be used to support ongoing initiatives from UN-Habitat’s programme of work in order to strengthen UN-Habitat’s capacity to support the implementation and monitoring of the 2030 Agenda and New Urban Agenda. This project document details outcomes and planned activities in order to ensure transparency and accountability in the use of the German funding, and to be able to report on the impact achieved through this support.
